Status: DONE (deployed and technically verified; new visual approval not claimed)
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoyAdvance/issues/16
Milestone: Keep pressed controls physically visible and naturally lit
Dependencies: 07_REFERENCE_SHAPE, 10_DARK_ROOM
Purpose: Correct the user's reported black D-pad and unrealistic action-button
  press lighting without disguising the problem with artificial illumination.

Tasks:
- [x] Inspect actual moving cap/socket geometry and reproduce pressed light loss.
- [x] Replace solid raised socket lids with beveled shell apertures.
- [x] Put receiving floors below the face for A/B, Start/Select and D-pad.
- [x] Preserve materials, travel, tilt, mapped input, lamp and LCD lighting.
- [x] Verify real aperture depth and rendered rest/press pixels for all front
  buttons and all four D-pad directions, including unlit caps.
- [x] Deploy through normal full gates and independently verify the live site.
- [x] Publish reviewed original live evidence and final documentation afterward.

Acceptance criteria:
- Moving caps do not disappear into raised socket lids.
- Gaps are actual recessed shell openings, not dark discs above the face.
- Pressed faces retain plausible illumination; no press-only glow or material
  color swap masks occlusion. Existing lamp shadows and LCD behavior remain.
- Native keyboard/remap/pointer behavior and physical travel stay intact.
- Existing inspection, power, reduced motion and responsive scene checks pass.

Completion evidence:
- Original geometry fails the actual D-pad illumination regression: sampled
  pressed brightness 123.63 versus 245.4 resting at one arm probe.
- All ten units, syntax/build PASS; focused Edge new/input pair 24.4s and
  expanded new/lamp pair 15.1s PASS.
- Four explicit-software scene/input/light/geometry cases PASS in 1.4m.
- Source 706563fe0355d6455a3c1ba1ff8fd9bafd3fa2a4 / Pages 41770495917:
  build, both complete browser shards (29 cases) and actual deployment PASS.
- Independent live verification matches all 23 exact assets and passes both
  real pressed-control and native input/LCD/power cases in 26.0s.
- Reviewed docs/images/pressed-controls.png crops actual deployed A/up captures.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-04: User reports both action-button and D-pad press lighting wrong.
  Raised solid sockets intersect caps; the front face has no control apertures.
  Cut openings with clearance and move socket surfaces below the face.
- 2026-11-04: First deterministic probe fixture accidentally triggers renderer
  recovery throttling and reads an empty frame. Correct the fixture tick, not
  production throttling, then establish the real failing original baseline.
- 2026-11-04: Preserve existing cap materials and motion; do not add emissive
  light or disable cap/shell shadows. Live release precedes final documentation.
